description:
Reader-only foundation for regular, already-published test fixtures. This ticket creates no recursive production Ty and adds no second type representation.

The existing #[cfg(test)] intern_two_phase fixture may construct a cycle solely to prove readers terminate; it remains test-only and deliberately does not establish production canonicality.

Guard the read/accumulation traversals with their semantic keys:
- has_vars and free_var_ids visit each Ty once;
- collect_subst_into visits each (pattern, witness, binding-side, target-side) relation once;
- collect_match_subst carries one in-flight matching relation per (pattern, witness, binding-side), treating a re-entered relation coinductively as already matched rather than marking a self-equal recursive pattern underconstrained;
- preserve the existing emptiness Memo's descriptor-keyed coinductive hypothesis with one negation-bearing-cycle proof.

Acceptance:
- self- and mutually-recursive test fixtures terminate;
- free-variable and substitution results are the finite fixed-point result, not a truncated tree walk;
- matching a recursive type against itself retains its established outcome;
- types_emptiness_discharges_a_negation_bearing_cycle proves the memo survives freshly composed descriptor arithmetic;
- all existing acyclic behavior remains unchanged.

Explicit non-goals: intersect, refine_widen, instantiation, closure erasure, runtime-envelope projection, addressed remapping, and convergence all construct new types. They must wait for the canonical regular-component commit ticket; a reserved or redirected Ty in any of them would violate the one-world identity law.
